Without data to reproduce the error, I have no way of tracking down the problem.  Are you using the latest development version (0.5-3.910) of semTools?

sessionInfo()

If not, install this in a fresh R session:

devtools::install_github("simsem/semTools/semTools")

Then restart R and try again.  First make sure each model converged by looking at each model's summary() output.  If you get the compareFit() error with all 4 models, try a pair at a time to figure out when the problem occurs.

