> This is unfortunately no longer the case with lavaan 6.07 and I
> encounter the following error message:
>
> Error in lavPredict(fit.h, newdata = sup.plus, type = "lv", method =
> "EBM",  :
>    lavaan ERROR: mismatch number of categories for some ordered variables
>          in newdata compared to original data.
> De plus : Warning message:
> In orig.ordered.lev - new.ordered.lev :
>    la taille d'un objet plus long n'est pas multiple de la taille d'un
> objet plus court.
>
> Do you know what this message means and how to fix it?
>
> Thank you very much by anticipation.
>
> Best regards,
>
> Jacques

Perhaps your variables need to be of class "ordered" in the new data?  It is not necessary to create a fake new row if you just repeat the original row:

sup <- rbind(sup, sup) # also convert to data.frame if necessary
for (nn in lavNames(fit, "ov.ord")) sup[nn] <- ordered(sup[nn]) # convert to ordered
lavPredict(fit, newdata=sup, ...)

If your error still occurs, please provide a reproducible example with data.  If you cannot provide your own data, it sounds simple enough to adapt the ?lavTables examples to do what you are trying to do, so the same problem should manifest.

