> The observed indicator is ordinal, so I don't yet have a confidence interval.

Ah right, because it is not an estimate.  Well, if you set std.lv <http://std.lv>=TRUE and use the default parameterization="delta", then the loadings will already be standardized.  In that case (assuming simple structure), a negative residual variance would occur if and only if your standardized loading exceeds +/- 1.  So you can check that CI to verify that it includes admissible values, which has the same implications for your model-implied residual variance.

