Dear Professor Terrence,

I hope you are very well.

My apologies for the late response. I’ve been busy.

Professor, I have several questions related to both the use of measEq.syntax function for testing measurement invariance and the use of CFA for comparing latent variable means across groups.

Question 1

When evaluating measurement invariance with categorical data, it’s strictly necessary to constrain threshold before constraining the factor loadings or can I constrain both parameters at the same time? More explicitly, must I test measurement invariance in this specific order “configural, thresholds, loadings, intercepts, residuals” or can I test it by analyzing the sequence “configural, thresholds and loadings, intercepts, residuals”?

Question 2

This question is related to the previous one. I’m currently evaluating measurement invariance in three different psychometric scales. By doing so, I get findings that I don't understand and I don't know if these results are due to an error from my part. Specifically, in one scale the degrees of freedom (and all the fit indexes) from the configural model and the model with thresholds constrained are exactly the same. Nonetheless, this doesn’t happen when comparing the configural and thresholds constrained models in the two other inventories. Is this normal? Is it something that can happen or is it due to an error?

Question 3

When declaring the data as categorical using the argument ordered in measEq.syntax function, is it necessary to declare again the data as categorical in cfa command from lavaan? For example:

syntax03 <- measEq.syntax(configural.model = fda.model, data = fda.data, ordered = paste0("x", 1:23),

                          ID.fac = "std.lv <http://std.lv>", ID.cat = "Wu.Estabrook.2016", parameterization = "theta", group = "sex",

                          group.equal = c("thresholds","loadings"))

metric.fit <- cfa(metric.model, data = fda.data, ordered = paste0("x", 1:23), parameterization = "theta",

                  group = "sex")

Question 4

When declaring the data as categorical using the argument ordered in measEq.syntax function, I must omit the estimator argument to avoid error messages or using both commands produce no errors? What do you suggest? For example:

syntax03 <- measEq.syntax(configural.model = fda.model, data = fda.data, ordered = paste0("x", 1:23),

                          ID.fac = "std.lv <http://std.lv>", ID.cat = "Wu.Estabrook.2016", parameterization = "theta", group = "sex",

                          group.equal = c("thresholds","loadings"), estimator = “WLSMV”)

metric.fit <- cfa(metric.model, data = fda.data, ordered = paste0("x", 1:23), parameterization = "theta",

                  group = "sex", estimator = “WLSMV”)

Question 5

How can I compare the latent variable means between groups (i.e. countries, sex, race) using multigroup confirmatory factor analysis? Do you have any tutorial for lavaan?

Thank you very much, professor. Sorry again for the inconvenience.

