Notice also the positive chi-square value, despite the model being saturated, with DF = 0. If you request fit indices, you will see that the reported chi-square for your target model is the same as the reported chi-square for the null model. So the zero covariance here is the covariance value for the null model. The question is, why is lavaan reporting fit and parameter estimates for the null model instead of the target model?

