I'm sure Yves could weigh in with more detail, I'll say from my experience if your estimates of variances are >10,000 that's the point where things get odd. Also, the issue isn't simply the size of the variances, but also the differences in scaling (e.g. if you have two variables with variances of .01 and 100 that can be an issue too, though in that case lavaan gives you a warning). One other note: this is not a lavaan specific issue, it's an issue for maximum likelihood.

