https://ademos.people.uic.edu/Chapter15.html#5_moderated_mediation_analyses_using_%E2%80%9Clavaan%E2%80%9D_package

But I am stuck here:

#Mean of centered alex (for use in simple slopes)
#This is making a coefficient labeled "alex.c.mean" which equals the intercept because of the "1"
#(Y~1) gives you the intercept, which is the mean for our .c variable

alex.c ~ alex.c.mean*1

Since this model includes observed variables and I have latent variables in my model:

1) I should I use double mean centering instead of mean centering in indProd?

2) Should I center predictor items and moderator items as well? or will it suffice to double mean center their interaction term only? (in indprod)

Gratefully,
Nino

