Hi, I
have conducted a daily diary study and my data consists of almost 110
individuals with 9 day observations each.

I have 1 predictor, 3 mediators, 1 outcome variable.

And I'm more interested in between-person level.

Q1. If
I want to test level 2 only, what should I do?

I
found an instruction about having level 1 model only (below) from your homepage
but not sure how to do in my case..

(from https://lavaan.ugent.be/tutorial/multilevel.html)

if you
do not have a model in mind for level 2, you can specify a saturated level by
adding all variances and covariances of the endogenous variables (here: y1, y2
and y3):

model <- '

level:
1

fw =~
y1 + y2 + y3

fw ~
x1 + x2 + x3

level:
2

y1 ~~
y1 + y2 + y3

y2 ~~
y2 + y3 y3 ~~ y3

'

Q2.

The
reason why I’m asking this question is because I got the following warning messages
about all my within-person indicators for some individuals(clusters):

Level-1 variable “r1” has no variance within some
clusters. The cluster ids with zero within variance are: A1, …

Level-1 variable “r2” has no variance within some clusters. The cluster ids with zero within variance are: A1, …

…

And the
summary(fit) printed standard errors which are all NA.

Any help would be greatly appreciated, thanks!!

